<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: UK PM Andy Burnham faces MPs for first time since taking office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38f19c4505888aef9a8ff9f776888837275c9a8ccc0ab70a8c79c13cab283cc7</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:21:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-mps-for-first-time-since-taking-office" /><summary type="html">The United Kingdom's new Prime Minister Andy Burnham will face lawmakers in the House of Commons on Tuesday for the first time since taking office six weeks ago. Burnham has promised to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of predecessor Keir Starmer, who announced Tuesday that he would resign his seat in Parliament after 11 years.Watch his speech live on FRANCE 24 at 15:30pm (GMT+2).</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Expert warns of 'hotter summers, more wildfires, more drought and more floods'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddfc4f08f4e0f5c73ec5659edc0cfc5e961dd1c738d9ddf55f279f17783e8b8b</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:24:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260901-expert-warns-of-hotter-summers-more-wildfires-more-drought-and-more-floods" /><summary type="html">One of the world's leading climate scientists has spoken to FRANCE 24 about the extreme heat events of this summer, and in the wake of the catastrophic flooding in Nepal, how other similar events are all but inevitable. Diana Ürge-Vorsatz is professor of environmental studies at the Central European University and vice-chair of the UN's Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Tupac murder trial: Ex-gang leader found guilty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec5b86c8c299724357f5331298ab58bd9b14ea317dd4ab417b0097f1ecd73c88</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T11:31:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-tupac-murder-trial-ex-gang-leader-found-guilty-1" /><summary type="html">Ex-street gang leader Duane "Keffe D" Davis was found guilty of the murder of hip-hop star Tupac Shakur at a Nevada court on Monday, three decades after the rapper was gunned down in a drive-by shooting in Las Vegas. Davis will face a maximum sentence of life in prison without the possibility of parole at his sentencing on October 13.</summary></entry><entry><title>As capital goes back to normal, Niger downplays soldiers' mutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66709b61d3d151a55781856c3482ec3a7759193f10132c7db8e705de0566d7c3</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:51:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-as-capital-goes-back-to-normal-niger-downplays-soldiers-mutiny" /><summary type="html">Niger's capital is back to normal after an intense week-end. A soldier mutiny took over Niamey on August 29, which was stopped by the army alongside the Russian paramilitary Africa Corps. The next day, Algeria sent four fighters aircrafts and two other military planes as cooperation with Nigeria is recently back on : an unexpected decision. Since it got independence, Algeria's non intervention doctrine is part of its DNA. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard tells us more about the goal of this decision.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Massive' Russian missile, drone attacks on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b389d84c0e38daac61236e7700d772d7ddc786d6f12efb009524e223f6fc33e</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:50:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-massive-russian-missile-drone-attacks-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured several more in Kyiv early on Tuesday, authorities said, in the sixth consecutive day of strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Russia, which began its full-scale invasion of its smaller neighbour in 2022, has escalated its air attacks in recent months, as gains made on the ground have slowed.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘This is systemic’: Parents demand accountability over child abuse in French childcare system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ae418927ef8133de788719a3eab845ade500bd702e3f86e3fca14a3b9ee6422</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:18:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/this-is-systemic-parents-demand-accountability-over-child-abuse-in-french-childcare-system" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Anne, the co-founder of SOS Périscolaire in French. She argues that the controversy surrounding France’s after-school childcare system should be understood as a systemic failure of institutional accountability on the local level. The fragmented structure becomes particularly consequential when warnings about violence are known but fail to produce adequate institutional change. The result, she argues, is a system in which children may speak clearly, repeatedly, or even physically through behavioural changes, yet still struggle to be heard by institutions designed to protect them.</summary></entry><entry><title>Back-to-school season in France sees tighter rules on mobile phones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1384fc1fec335a2f052d1ea6931850feabab556e42a02b2f1cde31edc7e5a6f3</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260901-back-to-school-season-in-france-sees-tighter-rules-on-mobile-phones" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, September 1: It's back-to-school season in France, this time with tighter rules on mobile phones. In other news, local opposition to data centres across the US and Europe could be a spanner in the works of the AI revolution. Finally, in footballing news, Lionel Messi retires from the Argentinian national team, and some English men play football in a river.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia's iconic Sidi Bou Said town added to UNESCO world heritage list</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6336d4704ce36ffeceb9edc9366d0c2c1757eb91c9c4c0e88e24a3070c23e13</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:07:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tunisia-s-iconic-sidi-bou-said-town-added-to-unesco-world-heritage-list" /><summary type="html">In Tunisia, UNESCO recognised the town of Sidi Bou Said as a world heritage site this July. The designation marks a new period in the cultural preservation of this historic tourist site. The special status may help as it battles erosion, like in the floods this last January, but it will also help boost its lesser known Sufi mystical traditions. FRANCE 24's Lilia Blaise and Hamdi Tlili were there to report on the Kharja ceremonies, which run in the town from mid-august til the end of September.</summary></entry><entry><title>A Hezbollah hideout stuffed with cash? Nope, this video was AI-generated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:980655e41987176b48708b13128ea648870f2da4bee9d37f6fc1faf62f2dc08d</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:01:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-hezbollah-hideout-stuffed-cash-ai-generated" /><summary type="html">A number of pro-Israel social media accounts have shared a video they claim shows wads of cash and stacks of gold bars in a cache belonging to a deceased Hezbollah leader. There's only one issue: the footage was created using AI. The original video was shared by an Egyptian satirical site.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Mobile phone ban greets French teenagers going back to high school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab02776d09295de1481842036d01273990cd0f2997bdccfc205a1959dc68fbda</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:00:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mobile-phone-ban-greets-french-teenagers-going-back-to-high-school" /><summary type="html">Millions of teenagers are going back to school in France, with one major change: mobile phones are now banned in high school, in a bid by the government to improve pupils to focus on their study, as it is concerned that passing too much time on their phone is arresting their development. But for schools, a major issue is how the measure can effectively be implemented.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal races to find hundreds stuck in hydropower tunnels following floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69cd3b5212d308c018ba024da7b928e191d2defa1b5c167ec02813c438c08ed8</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:53:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-races-to-find-hundreds-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-following-floods" /><summary type="html">More than 1,000 people have been killed in the devastating floods that struck the border between Nepal and Tibet. Authorities have started mass burials for unclaimed bodies while they wait for victims' families to claim them. Meanwhile, rescue operations are underway to rescue hundreds of workers stuck in hydropower tunnels. FRANCE 24's Shahzaib Wahlah tells us more from the Chitwan district in Nepal.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia fired over 2,800 drones at Ukraine in August amid war tactic change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95f995ba4470ba6b634a2810f37a243fef353c43fe54f9d010e1fb122416953b</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-fired-over-2-800-drones-at-ukraine-in-august-amid-war-tactic-change" /><summary type="html">Over the course of the month of August, Russia launched more than 2,800 jet-propelled drones at Ukraine, a type of drone that is harder to shoot down. That has come with a massive uptick in the number of drones used, considerind those now found on the frontline are quite a new model: Ukrainian authorities say they are pressed into service almost immediately after leaving the factory. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry looks at those new drones, and how Russia is using them to try and change the course of the war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia targets Kyiv and its region for sixth consecutive night of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fe595ceda1b780b0881c838a86fb7b216074fe8114047291aa28cca7635b311</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:39:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-targets-kyiv-and-its-region-for-sixth-consecutive-night-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">At least nine people have been killed and 14 injured in Russian strikes on Ukraine overnight. Moscow targeted Kyiv and the wider region in the attack, hitting a railway depot in the Kyiv. Russia's defence ministry said it had also struck infrastructure in the Southern Odesa region. Russia has intensified strikes on the beleaguered Ukrainian cities in recent weeks disrupting the daily lives of millions of people and triggering up to a dozen air-raid alerts a day.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu's wife shares conspiracy claim that opposition leader knew of Oct 7 attacks in advance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86f2537ad0566b982f1fd51a90ae5d18a1d3e372062d7465e53a736a6ce9a97f</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:36:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-netanyahu-s-wife-shares-conspiracy-that-opposition-leader-had-early-knowledge-of-oct-7-attacks" /><summary type="html">As Israel prepares for what are expected to be close-fought parliamentary elections in October, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's wife Sara on Monday shared a conspiracy theory that centre-left opposition figure Yair Golan had advance warning of the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Former gang member found guilty of murdering rapper Tupac Shakur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44865322247f9193d25603d1067afed5a72c4c9fb8f965733c96a1a414c11986</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/former-gang-member-found-guilty-of-murdering-rapper-tupac-shakur" /><summary type="html">A jury found Duane “Keffe D” Davis guilty of orchestrating the 1996 killing of rap icon Tupac Shakur, finally bringing a measure of resolution to a case that had gripped hip-hop fans and lingered in the public imagination for decades. Davis could be sentenced to life in prison following that verdict. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet tells us more about the verdict.</summary></entry><entry><title>Grand Canyon rescue operation still ongoing to find missing person after floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b9e588781476cfdaae4973de1084e40fef6f150b5df5bdabbcb4eb214d268df</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:24:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-grand-canyon-rescue-operation-still-ongoing-to-find-missing-person-after-floods" /><summary type="html">Only one person remains missing after the flash flood that claimed two lives in the Grand Canyon -  one of the most famous tourist attractions in the western United States. The force of the water destroyed much of the park's infrastructure,  including the only water pipeline supplying the Canyon. Over 80 people were rescued over the weekend.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentina: Lionel Messi announces end of international career</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e6202bf950cba246b4de47c0842abb2a947d286677da5757e189a0e99252505</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T08:23:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260901-argentina-lionel-messi-announces-end-of-international-career" /><summary type="html">Lionel Messi has announced his retirement from international football after 207 appearances for Argentina. With 125 goals to his name, he is by far the top scorer in his national team’s history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Lake Annecy gun linked to unsolved 2012 murder of British family in French Alps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f63c0d99b990102c1859612cab8ca501fa6b3cb930a544fec82387c996f5803e</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T08:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-lake-annecy-gun-linked-to-unsolved-2012-murder-british-iraqi-family-french-alps-chevaline" /><summary type="html">French officials say a Luger pistol fished out from the bottom of Lake Annecy shows similarities to the weapon used in the notorious 2012 killings of a British-Iraqi family and a French cyclist in the nearby village of Chevaline, opening up a new lead in a case that has befuddled investigators for over a decade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Glaciers in Himalayas retreating': Nepal floods triggered by 'glacier collapse &amp; massive landslide'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c033ae7d888b3a18bd574c692fac59b1b2757fda8dabe6611a96b4094ca7e12</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:26:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-glaciers-in-himalayas-retreating-nepal-floods-triggered-by-glacier-collapse-massive-landslide" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Joseph Shea, Glaciologist and Associate Professor at the University of Northern BC. Shea argues that the catastrophe should be understood as a compound event in which a glacier failure and a massive landslide occurred together. His analysis places the disaster within the broader, well-established transformation of the Himalayas under climate change. As warming changes high-mountain environments, scientists may increasingly need to identify subtle precursors to rare but potentially devastating cascading hazards.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Deadly Russian air attack hits energy and rail infrastructure in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffb14e4efc0c585adfb2d2831c69149055ac7707764363a3a42e45164d2ca941</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-deadly-russian-air-attack-hits-railway-depot-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian ballistic missile strikes apparently targeting energy and railway infrastructure rained down on Kyiv and surrounding areas in the early hours of Tuesday, Ukrainian authorities said, killing at least 12 people. It's the sixth consecutive day of Russian strikes on Ukraine's capital. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Government air strikes kill 20 alleged guerrillas in Colombia, president says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d823bb567f64813ba63741dc3966e487c832524331a018b99c1b97cce42b586</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T05:42:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-government-air-strikes-kill-20-alleged-guerrillas-in-colombia-president-says" /><summary type="html">Fresh government air strikes have killed 20 alleged members of the Central General Staff (EMC) armed group in southern Colombia, the country's new right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella said Monday. The new administration carried out two other deadly air strikes against suspected guerrillas in August, which sources within Colombia's forensics authority say killed at least four minors.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Sea change: Much of the world's economic GDP has moved to the Asia-Pacific region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8b7455d0c54295faef38b24931e0c1ef3971ab8f3d57dd9d7a27b9b7324f941</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T05:22:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260901-sea-change-much-of-the-world-s-economic-gdp-has-moved-to-the-asia-pacific-region-rana-mitter" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Rana Mitter, historian, author and ST Lee Chair in US-Asia Relations at the Harvard Kennedy School. He discusses the significance of the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) as it pertains to the evolution of a changing international system, this as the bloc holds a summit in Kyrgyzstan's capital Bishkek.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Oil prices extend gains as US-Iran tensions flare again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66073fa98b65ba95e539d1029303598454d1a152deabbfa8e137230866324d25</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T03:38:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again" /><summary type="html">Oil prices rose further Tuesday as renewed military exchanges between the United States and Iran, coupled with Donald Trump’s vow to hit Tehran “hard,” fueled fears of a broader escalation after weeks of relative calm. Follow our live blog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv kills at least eight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78a01f64e3521948874c3e5313298a2a5eab575d2cffee65865003d61910a03c</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T02:26:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four" /><summary type="html">A massive Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv and its surrounding region killed at least eight people and wounded more than a dozen overnight, Ukrainian officials said Tuesday, as children prepared to return to school amid heightened fears of further strikes.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
